WEBVTT

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.570
There exists a model of the seal Rin guards,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.060
created at 1/100th scale...

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.550
You could say it's a replica seal.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.790
What does it contain, Prontea-san?

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.790
There are two thousand
cockroaches trapped inside.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:27.340
Huh?

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.700
Making it a very dreadful seal indeed.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.880
Okay, then...

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.400
So, is it possible for a third party
to remove the seal?

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:42.390
This part here with the flag acts like
an antennae that maintains the sealing.

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:46.030
Destroy this and what's
inside comes spilling out.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.420
Does it?

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.810
Rin-san must think so too,
which explains why she's spent

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.630
eight centuries guarding the seal.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.190
And yet...

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.530
Hey, wait a sec! You're gonna
get roaches everywhere!

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.710
Here's what actually happens.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.950
They're all dead?

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.250
The exact cause of death is starvation.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.440
This isn't like cryogenics, where they'd be

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.260
preserved in a near-death state.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.580
It's just the same as how
roaches die in a few days

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.480
if left stuck inside a trap.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.760
The same applies to demons.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:46.740
They wouldn't last a year.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.750
They've all been dead for the last 799 years.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.620
Frankly, the previous Idaten
threw their lives away.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.370
If they'd maintained the seal
in shifts over a year,

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:53.080
that would've done it.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.520
But that never occurred to Rin-san
or the other Idaten.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.610
Well, I don't particularly see the problem.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:01.530
This means that breaking the seal
won't give the demons any advantage.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.850
On the contrary, that mistake
gave rise to the Demon Lord.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.870
Thinking about it now,
that doctor defies logic.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.700
How in the world does he have
a machine that can mimic

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:08.870
human expression and body language perfectly?

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.390
Much less an interface
complex enough for all that?

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.570
Are things like perspiration and blinking
synchronized to his own body?

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:13.690
That's not possible with current tech.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:15.280
There's only one method
I can think of that could

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.260
pilot such an elaborate device.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.800
The very same one you use, Prontea-san...
Thought control.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.260
Wait, what are you saying, Ysley-kun?
That the Demon Lord is an Idaten?

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.120
I confirmed with General Piscalat

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:30.860
that the demons found us by hacking
cameras all over the country.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.000
And you would have to be
an Idaten to hack cameras

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.190
that aren't connected to the internet.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:42.820
I think I'll skip the foreplay
and just come out and ask...

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.280
What exactly are you?

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:50.000
What's this, Miku? Are you doubting me?

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.080
Well, let's say that I'm very
interested in your identity.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.340
I think you're the first one
to actually express their suspicions.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:01.470
Maybe the Demon Lord is an Idaten?

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:05.970
Paula's wild guess about
the Demon Lord being an Idaten

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.970
based on the thoughts of demons
wasn't actually very far off the mark.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.230
Three things are necessary
for an Idaten to manifest.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:14.820
The thoughts of a number of creatures,
their desire for salvation,

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.360
and a period of time
numbering in the centuries.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.170
Take the Idaten who sacrificed themselves

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.660
and the thoughts of the slowly,
painfully dying demons...

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.990
Add 800 years to the mix,

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:27.400
and on the other side of the seal,
you've got the perfect storm.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.310
The dying demons' desperation created him

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.400
with the desire to protect demonkind,

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.340
while the Idaten who sacrificed themselves

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.830
were the source of his knowledge.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:39.800
It's no matter. Feel free to probe
around all you like.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.720
And if you do get an answer,
by all means, share it with me.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:46.050
Since I have no idea myself.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.030
Because they were disassembled
and reassembled,

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:51.440
his memories are extremely hazy.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.810
He's also physically unable
to leave the barrier.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.850
But he doesn't even realize this fact.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.280
Thus he projects his thoughts

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:01.570
and only interacts with the
outside world via machinery.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.650
That's the true nature of the Demon Lord.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:08.910
So, what now, Ysley-kun?

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:12.940
We know where to find him...
Are we going to go kill the Demon Lord?

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:14.710
Or no?

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.800
His attacks are fast, but light.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.010
Which means...

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:30.260
In this position, I can attack you freely

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:33.310
and you don't have the
strength to escape. I win.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.380
Shut it! This isn't over yet—

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:41.650
No, seriously, you lose.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.940
You've got good reflexes and speed.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:49.320
But even if you land those attacks,
they're not gonna hurt!

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.000
How about this?!

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:03.470
You stupid or something?

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:06.030
It doesn't matter how fast you come at me.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:08.810
If it's in a straight line,
landing a counter is easy.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:11.470
Looks like that's it.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:15.710
Damn... I had no idea I was this weak.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:17.820
What the shit have I been doing?

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:21.480
You seem troubled, my boy!

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:26.970
That's creepy as hell!
What're you doin' down there?!

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:31.990
Shouldn't you be asking about
how to attack with more power?

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:33.490
Okay...

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:35.660
Very good! Allow me to explain.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:37.660
What's this supposed to be?

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.490
Just what it looks like. A scale.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:41.420
Hop on, Paula.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.700
Okay...

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:49.190
It says 36 kilos. So what's the big idea?

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:52.140
Now try reducing your weight to zero.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:54.510
Like this?

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:00.850
Well, that explains how you're so good
at moving without making a sound.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:02.860
Doing this allows you
to move silently and swiftly,

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:03.730
as well as scale walls and ceilings.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:05.650
Now, want to land heavier attacks?
Just make yourself heavier instead!

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:07.700
As you can see, Idaten can defy
the laws of physics governing things

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:08.550
like mass and air resistance.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:09.250
Even in combat!

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:10.080
Reduce your mass to accelerate,

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.010
then increase it several tons
when you strike.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:12.760
Easy as pie.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:14.760
All Idaten are capable of
making themselves lighter.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.850
Even Hayato, who has trouble moving silently,

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:16.780
can reduce himself to 1 or 2 kilos.

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:18.250
But "getting heavier" is a separate matter.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.130
In order to vastly exceed your
base mass requires a level of

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:22.750
sophisticated mental imaging comparable
to projecting a weapon from your body.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.750
Reaching several tons would
take hundreds of years,

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:25.870
but a couple hundred kilos?
Only a couple years.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:26.930
A few dozen kilos? A few weeks.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:27.720
In the best case,

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:28.420
maybe even a few days.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.260
I think Paula might be able
to manage it now to some extent.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.560
Hey, it worked! I can get up to 90!

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:37.520
All right, let me give this a try.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:42.350
I've got a baseline of 65,
and then... I get heavier.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.060
It didn't change at all, damn it!

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.300
Because you were only flexing just now.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:53.450
You need to imagine what you're
trying to make happen. Picture it.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.420
Okay, let's try this.

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:00.120
Now, Hayato-kun,

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:04.340
take in the the pressure on your legs
and the ground right now.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:08.250
Then imagine all that weight is yours.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.320
Prontea-san...

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:11.840
Oh, Ysley-kun!

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.610
It's been less than a week
since Zoble attacked us.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.140
Is this training going to have any effect?

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:21.230
Well, if it doesn't, we can leave
Hayato out of the coming battles

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.750
and I'll train him over a longer period,

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:26.400
since we're going to be fighting
the Demon Lord eventually.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.290
Are we going to go kill him? Or no?

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.690
Let's not.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:35.000
The idea of an opponent who's a mixture
of a number of Idaten and demons...

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.490
We don't yet know how strong he might be.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.910
You think he'd pose a threat
even if Master and I fought together?

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.480
It's a simple matter
of not being absolutely certain.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:47.930
But one thing I know for sure is that

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:51.310
the Demon Lord isn't building
his strength in there.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:54.550
In other words, we can leave him be
and he won't get any stronger in the interim.

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:58.570
Okay, so you want to put
the biggest problem on hold

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.820
and use that extra time
to come up with a perfect plan?

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:03.930
Can't say it's my style...

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.320
If you want to fight that badly,
I won't stop you,

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:10.470
but <i>you'll</i> have to be the one to
convince Rin-san to break the seal.

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:11.530
Moreover,

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:14.890
Rin-san will be free to go wherever
she likes once the seal is no more.

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:18.700
You're right! We should make sure we're
fully prepared for whatever might happen!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:24.150
That said, we will<i> have to fight
the Demon Lord eventually...</i>

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:30.450
I wonder if I have to train, too...
What a drag! I just wanna do research!

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:33.800
Damn it! How long am I supposed
to carry this thing?!

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:37.310
Until your body memorizes
the feeling of its weight!

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:41.260
If you're still thinking of it at "carrying,"
then you're going about this all wrong!

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:48.840
Okay, try that again while
increasing your weight.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:51.150
I'll tell you how different it comes out.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.170
Going from 36 kilos to 90 kilos...

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.980
That should be twice as powerful!

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:05.170
That was heavier, yeah,
but you weren't going as fast.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:09.970
I think the trick is to only get
heavy for the moment of impact.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:13.620
That's kind of a big ask, y'know...

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:16.210
Even for someone who's a natural
at lowering her weight,

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:18.890
increasing it in an instant
seems to be difficult.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:22.390
When I think about how long this'll
take to be viable in combat,

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.400
it makes my head hurt...

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:26.230
He's making them do this
knowing full well

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:28.480
that they won't be able
to pull it off, isn't he?

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:36.260
How the hell am I supposed
to learn this shit?!

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:43.370
Hey, General Piscalat! Come fight me again!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.700
I don't mind, but...

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.910
Good grief, this boy has no patience.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:54.170
From the look of it,
I doubt this will go any differently.

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:56.930
He doesn't seem to have learned a thing.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.930
Gotta make my body heavy...

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:04.810
Just like that rock!

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.650
Wh-What was that?

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:22.560
Whoa, holy shit!

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:25.450
That really was way stronger!

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.050
Prontea-san, you're awesome, man!

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:31.180
Uh, yeah, thanks...

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:34.000
Seriously, you're awesome!

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:33.470
How the...?

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.430
I'm up next.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:42.930
You're gonna have to prove
that wasn't a fluke just now.

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:45.890
Fine by me! Bring it on!

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.560
Th-This is...

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:57.990
He's able to chain attacks even
though that's far more difficult.

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:01.040
That boy... Is he actually a prodigy?

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:04.570
I think I understand.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:10.500
It may be that Hayato has never thrown
a punch at his natural body weight.

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:15.000
This is actually kind of convenient...

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:18.600
He might be increasing his weight
more than he's realizing as a result.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:21.950
Prontea-san?

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:24.340
Yeah, you're right!

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:27.310
Hey, wait, is this for real?

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:31.730
Then all of his previous attacks were
thrown at only a few kilograms?

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:39.070
Which means he's gotten this<i>
strong in just eighty years...</i>

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:41.900
That's even harder to believe!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:51.720
Not bad...

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:55.220
There's room for improvement,
but you win, kid.

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:57.120
Hell yeah!

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:59.360
So this is the kind of power that
an Idaten who grows up

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:02.340
earnestly yearning
for strength can achieve...

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:07.050
All right, next up is all three
of you at once, right?

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.440
Hope you two weren't
expecting a nice, long break!

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:12.270
No, that won't be necessary, Hayato-kun.

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:14.830
I'll be your opponent this time.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:20.070
This probably suits him better
than holding up a boulder.

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:23.860
I'm going to fight normally,
with one handicap:

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.950
I won't dodge any of your attacks.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:30.200
Your goal is to manage to damage me.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.530
Damn, you might be pretty awesome,

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:36.250
but you're still a royal pain
in the ass, y'know that?!

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.960
Don't screw with me!

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:56.290
Damn... I guess beating him
isn't gonna be easy after all...

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:58.020
Freaking monster...

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:00.360
He's so incredibly powerful...

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.320
Did we seriously intend to wage war
against someone like this?

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:05.450
It's a little late now, but that's terrifying.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:07.570
Piscalat-neechan...

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:11.240
We're due to report in. What should we do?

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:18.130
We've got two choices. We can keep quiet
or give a false report to buy time.

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:19.030
But...

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:31.090
Based on this footage alone,
they really don't seem that impressive.

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:35.770
There's something weird
about how weak this boy is.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:41.880
It's like he's actually much stronger,
but doesn't realize it somehow.

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:48.190
If he could utilize his full potential,
would be he be stronger than me?

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:52.620
I think you'd still have the edge, Brandy.

00:14:53.190 --> 00:14:56.620
Y-Yes, of course I would.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:15:00.650
But I'm pretty sure he
could beat the rest of us.

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:04.500
In fact, I think some of us
might already be lost...

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:07.340
What do you mean by that?

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:12.050
There's been no report from
Piscalat's group whatsoever.

00:15:12.270 --> 00:15:15.210
Miku will probably see through
any ruse we try to pull.

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:17.930
The smart call is simply to stay quiet.

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:21.410
Are the three of them dead already?

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:27.280
No, I bet that they've been
captured and squeezed for intel.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:28.330
Don't be ridiculous.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:32.340
Even if they were caught, I doubt Neput
and Piscalat would talk so easily.

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:37.790
I get the feeling Cory-kun would spill
the beans pretty quickly under torture.

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:41.370
Torturing Cory-kun...

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.970
And Piscalat's such a virgin, too...

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:46.500
Plus, when I think about Neput
on top of everything else...

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.070
God, I want some!

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:55.140
Brandy, my brain's not going to work
otherwise, so I need a bathroom break!

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:58.890
If you're going to the bathroom, then why
are you taking that filthy thing with you?!

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:01.050
Fine, I need a good ****!

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:02.690
Could you please not be so blunt?!

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:06.520
Honestly, she doesn't have a
trace of refinement...

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:09.940
But did they really lose?

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:12.730
Your Lordship? Darling?

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:13.410
Hmm?

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:14.940
Has there been any news?

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.580
None at all.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:19.530
There's been no contact
from Neput and the others.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:22.000
We can't even tell if they're a lost cause.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:26.770
With Nickel gone, you're our
strongest line of defense.

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:29.090
I'm counting on you, Brandy.

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:31.870
Yes. Leave it to me.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:38.700
Well, Miku, did you discover anything?

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:43.630
She's so focused and serious!

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:47.310
Is the situation really that dire?

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:49.590
It was actually just post-climax clarity.

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:56.760
Paula, if you're bored, would you like
to join me on a trip to Sarabael?

00:16:56.760 --> 00:17:01.860
It'd be easier for the two of us
to convince them that either alone.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:04.330
That's fine with me.

00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:13.860
Damn... I keep hitting him
and it's like he doesn't feel it...

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:17.560
You know, Hayato,
there's one other simple way

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:21.430
to increase your attack power
that doesn't involve your weight.

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:25.500
I wonder what he's filling
your head with now.

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:30.040
What's this all about?
And why all the secrecy?

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:31.090
Is something going on?

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:32.020
Mom?

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:36.070
No one knows that I've called you all here.

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:38.660
I'll get directly to the point.

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:42.620
I want the three of you to escape
the country immediately.

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:46.950
When you do, take a demon
of your choosing with you.

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:48.630
Any questions?

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:52.420
What for? And why are
we doing this in secret?

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:55.040
To prevent demonkind from being wiped out.

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:57.640
As things currently stand, Neput
and two others have been captured,

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.450
and since we have no way of knowing when
they might leak information about us,

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:03.060
I have no choice but to take
action on my own in secret.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:07.940
Why the three of us
and not our older siblings?

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:10.190
Well, that's because...

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:14.320
The three of you are the ones
I actually gave birth to.

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.940
Hey! What's so funny?

00:18:18.940 --> 00:18:21.750
Oh, I'm sorry, it's just...

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:25.020
You were talking about things like
preserving demonkind and intel leaks before

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:31.380
to justify it, but you really just
want to help your kids escape.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:37.180
And you're usually so rational!

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:39.930
I guess you've got a
maternal streak after all!

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.340
I had no idea!

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:46.810
Shut it! Just get out of the kingdom
before I kill you myself!

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.860
Okay, Mom.

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:50.940
We'll go. We'll run.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:53.940
Take care of yourself, too, okay?

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:56.190
Please be care...ful...

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:59.570
Yes. You three take care, as well.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:07.250
They didn't know I have
a maternal streak, huh?

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:08.980
Well, neither did I.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:11.500
Here you go!

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:14.130
Kuraishi-sama, you rock!

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.590
Ferlandia!

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:18.300
I've got a big trip coming up.
You should join me.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:21.130
I've got shit to do, unlike you.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:24.760
That means no time to join in
your playboy games.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:28.690
Look, just come with me.
Direct orders from Empress Brandy.

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:30.600
The rest of them are mere distractions.

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:33.690
Huh, so it's not just fun and games?

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:36.900
What is it, Buzz? You wanted to talk?

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:38.570
Uh, well...

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:40.800
Um, it's about...

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:42.510
Should I explain to her what's going on?

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:45.950
Or would it be more natural to tell her
how I feel and see what she says first?

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.710
Kroft!

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:51.660
Oh? What is it, Princess Raki?

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:54.430
Please! Take me away from this place!

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:59.880
This is just getting more depressing...

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:02.650
I don't wanna die yet.

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:08.010
I wanna run... I wanna run...

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:10.450
God...

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:15.980
If you're watching,
I beg you, send us salvation.

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:22.280
My devoted faithful, the world
is in need of salvation!

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:26.430
The Zoble Empire uses their military might
to commit every manner of barbarism!

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:30.910
Hotaena has forsaken God in favor
of indulging in wanton delights!

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:34.790
They are sinful nations whose
policy is to blaspheme God!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:38.430
They are in need of redemption
that only we can offer!

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.530
Yes, redemption in the form of death!

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:43.450
At this point, their only hope is for

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:47.140
their souls be purified at the hands of us,
God's humble servants!

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:48.870
Redemption for the devils!

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.560
Purification for the devils!

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.880
The finite wealth and resources of this world

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:57.240
cannot be monopolized
by such unholy authoritarians!

00:20:57.240 --> 00:20:59.420
Their management is a task

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:04.030
that only we, God's servants,
are fit to handle!

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:07.550
What the—?!

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:12.160
I've heard the rumors,
but that was a seriously pathetic sermon.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:16.540
Didn't it amount to "no one's
allowed to have power, except us"?

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.730
What are you impudent
children trying to say?!

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.420
And just who are you?!

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.940
Good afternoon. It's nice to meet you.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:24.250
We're gods!
